# One streamed answer. `mid` is taken while the fake gateway holds the stream
# after its first 30 events (slow-line-turn.json's `holdAt`: MARKER-HEAD and
# word0 to word28), so both binaries have read the same text and the activity
# row's out count is the same; `end` once the stream is let go and the turn
# has settled. A snap at a fixed second after Enter read a different chunk on
# each binary under load (PR #74's sweep, fx/xfx: 59/63, 63/61, 63/61, 61/59).
gateway slow-line-turn.json
wait 2
type stream please
key Enter
held
wait 1
snap mid
release
wait 6
snap end
